<header><h1>The Nekro Virus: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_nekro">The Nekro Virus</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="galactic-threat"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Galactic%20Threat">Galactic Threat</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nekro player makes their prediction during the same timing window as riders, after any &ldquo;when an agenda is revealed&rdquo; abilities, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Veto"><i>Veto</i></a> action card or the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s Quash faction ability. They must predict an outcome; abstaining is not an outcome.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does the Nekro make its Galactic Threat prediction, and what can it predict?&rdquo;: &ldquo;In the same window as riders: after &lsquo;when revealed&rsquo; effects such as Veto or Quash, before anyone votes. It predicts an outcome; abstaining isn&rsquo;t one.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player may still play rider action cards.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can a player who cannot vote (such as the Nekro Virus) play rider action cards? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does the Nekro make its Galactic Threat prediction &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Nekro may also play riders on the same or different outcomes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player has the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, the Nekro player may vote, without losing their ability to predict outcomes for their <sc>Galactic Threat</sc> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the speaker breaks a tie without casting any votes, then the speaker&rsquo;s technologies are ineligible to be gained.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Galactic Threat gain a technology if nobody voted for the predicted outcome?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; the Nekro gains a technology from a player who voted for that outcome. If it won through the speaker&rsquo;s tie-break &hellip; with no player voting for it, there is nobody to take from.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If no player casts votes, then no technology can be gained.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Galactic Threat gain a technology if nobody voted for the predicted outcome?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; the Nekro gains a technology from a player who voted for that outcome. If it won through the speaker&rsquo;s tie-break &hellip; with no player voting for it, there is nobody to take from.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="technological-singularity"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Technological%20Singularity">Technological Singularity</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Nekro player gains a technology during a space combat, this does not prevent them from gaining technology during ground combats in the <b>Invasion</b> step of the same tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If multiple ground combats happen on separate planets as part of a single <b>Invasion</b> step during one action, the Nekro player may gain a technology during each combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Any method that destroys a unit during combat will trigger <sc>Technological Singularity</sc>, including an anti&ndash;fighter barrage roll, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> faction technology, etc.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which kills trigger Nekro&rsquo;s Technological Singularity?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Anti-Fighter Barrage is part of combat and counts.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When the Nekro Virus gain a technology, does the other player lose it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It triggers when any opponent&rsquo;s unit is destroyed in combat, even one the Yin sacrifice with Devotion or one killed by Assault Cannon or Anti-Fighter Barrage.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This includes any method used by the Nekro player&rsquo;s opponent that destroys their own units, usually as an ability cost.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When the Nekro Virus gain a technology, does the other player lose it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;even one the Yin sacrifice with Devotion.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If a unit is removed, but not destroyed, that unit will not trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Infantry II trigger on infantry removed by the Jol-Nar agent?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; removing isn&rsquo;t destroying.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Space cannon and bombardment rolls happen outside of combat. Any hits produced cannot be used to trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which kills trigger Nekro&rsquo;s Technological Singularity?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Kills from Space Cannon, Bombardment, or structures destroyed when control is established don&rsquo;t count, since those happen outside combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player chooses to gain a unit upgrade technology, that upgrade will be in effect from that point in the combat onwards.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When the Nekro Virus gain a technology, does the other player lose it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it works immediately, even for the rest of that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The combat value of a combat dice is fixed as it is rolled, and all combat dice are rolled before any hits are assigned. Gaining a unit upgrade technology will not cause any already rolled combat dice to produce any additional hits due to an improved combat value. The same applies to unit ability dice.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Destroying an opponent&rsquo;s unit during the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step, and gaining a unit upgrade technology will allow units of that type to use the abilities and attributes of the upgrade for the combat rolls of the same round.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: the gained technology &ldquo;works immediately, even for the rest of that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Destroying an opponent&rsquo;s unit at the start of a combat, such as with the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology, and gaining a unit upgrade technology with an <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a> ability will allow units of that type to use that ability during the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step of the first round of combat.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: the gained technology &ldquo;works immediately, even for the rest of that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player uses the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy a unit when it uses its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, this will occur before any units are destroyed from being assigned hits. If the Nekro player then gains a technology that gives their units the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, they may then use that ability for their units participating in the combat to cancel hits produced by their opponent during that round of combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player destroys a unit, and gains a technology with an ability that is used during the same timing window, they may use that ability immediately.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When the Nekro Virus gain a technology, does the other player lose it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it works immediately, even for the rest of that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, if the Nekro player uses the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology at the start of a space combat to destroy a unit belonging to the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player, and thus place a Valefar token on that player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> faction technology, the Nekro player may immediately use the ability of their Valefar <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Ghosts_of_Creuss#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> to produce a hit against one of the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player gains the Infantry II unit upgrade from their <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability during a combat, any of the Nekro player&rsquo;s infantry destroyed at the same time as the unit used to trigger the <sc>Technological Singularity</sc> ability will be returned to their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Nekro player uses a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy an opponent&rsquo;s unit, and gain the Infantry II unit upgrade, then any infantry destroyed in that <b>Assign Hits</b> step will roll to be placed on the Infantry II card. This will most commonly occur if the Nekro player has infantry participating in space combat via the ability of their flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Any infantry destroyed by the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha">Strike Wing Alpha</a> II faction unit ability are destroyed during the <b>Roll Dice</b> substep of the <b>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</b> step. The Nekro player will not have the opportunity to gain the Infantry II unit upgrade until the <b>Assign Hits</b> substep immediately following, and so the destroyed infantry will be returned to their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot use <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=The%20Prophet%27s%20Tears"><i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i></a> relic to draw an action card when they gain a technology using this ability.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;They cannot do this when they GAIN technology via their Technological Singularity faction ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus use the Prophet&rsquo;s Tears relic?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; it triggers when you research a technology, which the Nekro never do.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="propagation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Propagation">Propagation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Nekro player may still resolve the secondary ability of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card, which will instead gain them command tokens. They must still spend a command token from their strategy pool and four resources to do so.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Nekro Virus pay normally to use the Technology secondary?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; like anyone they spend a strategy token and 4 resources, and because they can&rsquo;t research, Propagation gives them 3 command tokens instead.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player may still benefit from owning the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Sciences"><i>Minister of Sciences</i></a> agenda card.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If an ability triggers &ldquo;when&rdquo; a player researches a technology, that ability will still be triggered by the Nekro player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Nekro player owns <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=The%20Prophet%27s%20Tears"><i>The Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i></a> relic, they may draw an action card whenever they would research a technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus player use the Prophet&rsquo;s Tears Relic? A: Yes, when the Nekro virus player uses their Propagation faction ability, they could exhaust the Relic to gain an action card.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: <sup>2</sup> Conflicts: RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus use the Prophet&rsquo;s Tears relic?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; it triggers when you research a technology, which the Nekro never do, so it does nothing for them.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If an ability triggers &ldquo;after&rdquo; a player researches a technology, that ability will never be triggered by the Nekro player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Anti-Intellectual%20Revolution"><i>Anti&ndash;Intellectual Revolution</i></a> law is in play, the Nekro player will not destroy a ship when they would research a technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Anti-Intellectual Revolution work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Nekro are unaffected, since Propagation gains tokens instead of researching.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The Nekro player may play the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Reveal%20Prototype"><i>Reveal Prototype</i></a> action card, gaining three command tokens instead of researching, but only if there is a unit upgrade technology the card could research.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus play Reveal Prototype?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes, gaining 3 command tokens instead of the technology, but only if there&rsquo;s a valid unit upgrade the card could research.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, if the Nekro player&rsquo;s only units in the combat are dreadnoughts and fighters, and they already own both Dreadnought II and Fighter II, they cannot play <i>Reveal Prototype</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Example of the parent note.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="antivirus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Antivirus">Antivirus</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The effect of <i>Antivirus</i> does not prevent the Nekro player gaining a technology from a player via their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Galactic%20Threat"><sc>Galactic Threat</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The player holding <i>Antivirus</i> may only play it at the start of a combat they are participating in.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Nekro player does not need to be participating in that combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li><i>Antivirus</i> has no effect while it is in a player&rsquo;s hand.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Antivirus</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Nekro player this turn.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Nekro player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Antivirus</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Nekro player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Antivirus</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="valefar-assimilator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When copying another technology, each <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> may later be used to copy a different faction technology.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator?&rdquo;: &ldquo;two at a time, one per token; to copy a third you move a token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Should you switch from Exo to Super, and wanted Exo again later, you would &hellip; need to&rdquo; copy it again.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When copying another technology, <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> will retain its exhausted/readied state. It will not copy the target technology&rsquo;s exhausted/readied state.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The Nekro player may use any ability of the copied technology that does not require exhausting as a cost, even if the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card is exhausted.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>An exhausted <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> will always ready during the Status Phase, even if it is not currently copying a technology with an exhaust ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player would copy a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade, and they are already copying a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade of the same type, they must use the same Valefar Assimilator token; they lose the previous faction unit upgrade.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.21: &ldquo;If the Nekro Virus gains a unit upgrade technology of the same unit type as a unit upgrade technology they already have, the previous upgrade is removed, and they must use the same Valefar Assimilator token that was used to copy the previous upgrade.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens to the Nekro&rsquo;s own unit upgrades &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A second faction upgrade for the same unit replaces the first, using the same token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Generic technologies are never fully lost even if they are overwritten. Faction technologies, however, are.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot copy faction&ndash;specific units that have not been upgraded.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Units printed on faction sheets, like Muaat&rsquo;s Prototype War Sun I or flagships, aren&rsquo;t technologies and can&rsquo;t be copied.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.21 covers copying unit upgrade technologies only.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A faction&rsquo;s mech is not a technology. The Nekro player cannot use a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> to copy a mech.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 55.4: &ldquo;Mech unit cards are not technologies.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook: each player takes their faction&rsquo;s &ldquo;mech unit card.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a generic unit upgrade, and gains a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade, then the faction&ndash;specific version will be in effect. If the faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade is later lost, they revert to the generic unit upgrade.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus have both a standard and a faction-specific unit upgrade of the same type? A: Yes. Only the faction-specific unit upgrade technology will be in effect, but should the Nekro lose the faction-specific upgrade &hellip; they would revert to the standard unit upgrade technology.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;The copied faction upgrade covers your generic one, which you keep; only one is in effect.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The intent is not that that the generic upgrades are lost, in this case.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Owning two unit upgrades for the same type of unit in this manner only counts as one unit upgrade toward the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Develop%20Weaponry"><i>Develop Weaponry</i></a> and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_2:~:text=Revolutionize%20Warfare"><i>Revolutionize Warfare</i></a> objectives.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;If the Nekro Virus owns multiple unit upgrade technologies of the same type &hellip; does each one count toward the &lsquo;Develop Weaponry&rsquo; and &lsquo;Revolutionize Warfare&rsquo; objectives? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do technologies the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator count for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;But when a copied faction upgrade covers a generic one, like Dreadnought II, only one of the two counts.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Mar 7, 2018): &ldquo;That&rsquo;s correct, or at least, what is intended.&rdquo; Answer addresses Develop Weaponry; Revolutionize Warfare is the same unit-upgrade count.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player gains a faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology while they own the generic Infantry II unit upgrade technology and they have infantry on that unit upgrade card that would be placed in their home system at the start of their next turn, then those infantry are transferred to the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card that they are using to copy the faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a> flagship unit upgrade technology, its attributes and abilities replace those of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 97.1a: &ldquo;The Nekro Virus player may upgrade their units with units of the same type (e.g., &lsquo;dreadnought&rsquo; or &lsquo;infantry&rsquo;) even if those unit&rsquo;s names do not match.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 97.4: &ldquo;After a player gains a unit upgrade card, each of that player&rsquo;s units that correspond to that upgrade card is treated as having the attributes and abilities printed on that upgrade card. Any previous attributes of that unit, such as the one printed on that player&rsquo;s faction sheet, are ignored.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Units printed on faction sheets, like Muaat&rsquo;s Prototype War Sun I or flagships, aren&rsquo;t technologies and can&rsquo;t be copied (the Nomad&rsquo;s Memoria II card is the exception).&rdquo; Memoria II is the only copyable flagship upgrade.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_jol_nar">Jol&ndash;Nar</a> player uses their hero to replace a technology which is currently being copied by a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i>, it will remain copied with a Valefar Assimilator token on it while in that player&rsquo;s technology deck.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The token stays on the tech in the tech-deck and Valefar Assimilator still has that technology&rsquo;s text.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>For the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_4:~:text=Adapt%20New%20Strategies"><i>Adapt New Strategies</i></a> objective, a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> technology will count if and only if it is currently copying another technology.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do technologies the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator count for objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; a copied technology counts with its colour and type.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> FFG ruling (stephen986, Sep 19 2017): &ldquo;The intent was that after placing an assimilator token on another faction&rsquo;s faction specific technology, it would then count toward the secret objective.&rdquo; Counting only once a token is placed on another technology implies the if-and-only-if.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has copied certain technology (possibly two or more at different points in time), the following apply:<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If both the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade and the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Vortex"><i>Vortex</i></a> technology are copied, and another player blockades a Nekro space dock, the Nekro player returns any captured units, then destroys the blockaded space dock.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player has copied both the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Barony_of_Letnev#:~:text=Non-Euclidean%20Shielding"><i>Non&ndash;Euclidean Shielding</i></a> technology and the generic <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor"><i>Duranium Armor</i></a> technology, then a space combat between the Nekro player and the <a href="/F_letnev">Letnev</a> player in certain circumstances may result in neither player being able to win. If this happens, the attacker must declare a retreat. If the attacker cannot do so, they destroy all their units in that combat.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ, on combats that are &ldquo;impossible for either side to win&mdash;for example, certain configurations of ships using the &lsquo;Non-Euclidean Shielding&rsquo; and &lsquo;Duranium Armor&rsquo; technologies in concert? A: If neither side has the potential to win, the attacker must retreat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If both the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Magmus%20Reactor"><i>Magmus Reactor</i></a> technology and the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade are copied, the Nekro player may move their space docks into supernovae.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II unit upgrade is copied, both the Nekro player and the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player may have their space docks in the same system, if there are no ships in that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s Exotrireme II unit upgrade is copied, and the Nekro player is in a combat with the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player, then the players will alternate when resolving end of combat round abilities, starting with the active player (all players may resolve abilities in initiative order, but it is most common for only the two players involved in the combat to want to resolve abilities). For example, if the attacking player has two Exotriremes II in the system and the defender has four, assuming both players are hostile toward each other, the most likely sequence is as follows: The attacker activates one of their Exotriremes II, leaving them with one and the defender with two; The defender activates one of their Exotriremes II leaving them with one and the attacker with none.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_deepwrought">Deepwrought</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Radical%20Advancement"><i>Radical Advancement</i></a> technology is copied, the Nekro player may resolve its ability, and will gain the chosen new technology; they will not gain command tokens.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Nekro player may lose a technology if they copy a new one. If they lose certain technologies, the following apply:<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Nekro player loses the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> II, each space dock the Nekro player controls must be placed on a planet they control in the same system, or the space dock is returned to their reinforcements.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.19: &ldquo;If a Valefar Assimilator token is removed from the Saar &lsquo;Floating Factory&rsquo; unit upgrade, each of the Nekro Virus&rsquo; space docks must be placed on an eligible planet they control in that space dock&rsquo;s system, or the space dock is returned to their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Nekro player loses the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#War_Sun:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> II, and the Nekro player does not have the generic war sun technology, each of their war suns are removed from the game board.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.20: &ldquo;If a Valefar Assimilator token is removed from a war sun unit upgrade and the Nekro Virus player does not have the standard war sun unit upgrade, each of the Nekro Virus player&rsquo;s war suns are returned to their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Magmus%20Reactor"><i>Magmus Reactor</i></a> is lost, the Nekro player&rsquo;s units may remain in any supernovae they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What happens when the Nekro move a Valefar token off a technology their units depend on?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Ships already in a supernova after losing Magmus Reactor are fine.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Vidyaraja, Sep 18, 2017): &ldquo;Losing Magmus Reactor in a supernova has no effect on the ships in the supernova, as the effects of a supernova do not kill ships, only restrict or disallow movement.&rdquo; Units stay; restriction on moving in or through follows from the supernova rule.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> II is lost, the dimensional tear tokens are removed from under the Nekro player&rsquo;s space docks; the systems are no longer gravity rifts (unless the system tile is a printed gravity rift).<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>The Nekro player may lose a faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology, while they have infantry on the unit upgrade card that would be placed in their home system at the start of their next turn. If they are moving the Valefar Assimilator token to a different faction&ndash;specific infantry unit upgrade technology, the infantry remain on the <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> card. Else, if they own the generic Infantry II unit upgrade technology, the infantry are transferred to that unit upgrade card. Otherwise, the infantry are returned to the Nekro player&rsquo;s reinforcements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-alastor"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor">The Alastor</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Any effect that may target ships or non&ndash;fighter ships may target a ground force that is participating in space combat due to the effect of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Infantry that are participating in space combat due to the effects of &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; do count as ships (in addition to their own unit type) for the purpose of card effects. But, as a unit that can be transported, they do not count against fleet supply in that system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This includes counting toward the three non&ndash;fighter ships necessary to trigger the effect of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Do infantry involved in a space combat via the effects of &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; flagship count toward the ships required to use the &lsquo;Assault Cannon&rsquo; technology? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>The <a href="/F_winnu">Winnu</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Winnu#Flagship:~:text=Salai%20Sai%20Corian"><i>Salai Sai Corian</i></a>, will roll one dice for each infantry the Nekro player has participating in a space combat via the effect of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Does the Winnu &lsquo;Salai Sai Corian&rsquo; flagship get additional dice for infantry participating in a fight due to the Nekro &lsquo;Alastor&rsquo; flagship? A: Yes. The &lsquo;Salai Sai Corian&rsquo; would get one additional die per infantry.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Nekro ground forces fighting via the flagship count for other effects?&rdquo;: &ldquo;they count as non-fighter ships for things like the Winnu flagship&rsquo;s extra dice (per the LRR FAQ).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>After the Nekro player uses the ability of <i>The Alastor</i>, all other players will have the opportunity to resolve an &ldquo;at the start of combat&rdquo; or an &ldquo;at the start of a round of combat&rdquo; ability before the Nekro player may resolve another ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, say the Nekro player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology, and uses the ability of <i>The Alastor</i> to bring the total number of non&ndash;fighter ships in the combat to three (or more). Other players may then resolve one ability each. If their opponent uses an ability that destroys ships, such as from their own <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a>, to reduce the number of non&ndash;fighter ships the Nekro player has in the combat to two (or fewer), then the Nekro player will be unable to resolve the ability of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Some abilities may destroy <i>The Alastor</i> at the start of a combat before the Nekro player has used its ability, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon"><i>Assault Cannon</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ground forces on planets remain there while participating in combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Ground Forces participating in space combat via The Alastor do not move from their origin location. If they were on planets at the start of combat, they stay on the planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>When the Nekro player is in a space combat against the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player, their infantry on planets participating in the combat cannot be targeted by the ability of the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Destroyer:~:text=Strike%20Wing%20Alpha%20II"><i>Strike Wing Alpha II</i></a> destroyers.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If they were on planets at the start of combat, they stay on the planet, participate in combat, and are immune to SWA2&rsquo;s ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If <i>The Alastor</i> is destroyed during space combat, any ground forces in that combat remain in that combat.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Infantry that are committed to the space combat due to the effects of &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; continue to participate until the end of the combat, even if &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; is destroyed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology with one of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> technologies during a space combat, any ground forces in that combat remain in that combat. If the Nekro player starts the space combat copying another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology, ground forces cannot participate in that combat, unless the Nekro player stops copying that flagship unit upgrade technology during the &ldquo;start of combat&rdquo; window.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This applies only to copying another player&rsquo;s flagship unit upgrade technology, currently only the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a>, with a <i>Valefar Assimilator</i> X or Y token. Copying a flagship with <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Breakthrough:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator%20Z"><i>Valefar Assimilator Z</i></a> does not replace the abilities of <i>The Alastor</i>.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 97.4: &ldquo;After a player gains a unit upgrade card, each of that player&rsquo;s units that correspond to that upgrade card is treated as having the attributes and abilities printed on that upgrade card. Any previous attributes of that unit &hellip; are ignored.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What can the Nekro copy with Valefar Assimilator?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Units printed on faction sheets, like Muaat&rsquo;s Prototype War Sun I or flagships, aren&rsquo;t technologies and can&rsquo;t be copied (the Nomad&rsquo;s Memoria II card is the exception).&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With the Nekro breakthrough, can the flagship copy several other flagships, and what does it copy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;you may put an Assimilator Z token on their faction sheet instead, and your flagship gains that flagship&rsquo;s text abilities.&rdquo; Gains, in addition to its own.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Ground forces participating in a space combat due to the effect of <i>The Alastor</i> are units that can be transported, so they do not count toward the Nekro player&rsquo;s fleet pool limit.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Infantry that are participating in space combat due to the effects of &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; do count as ships (in addition to their own unit type) for the purpose of card effects. But, as a unit that can be transported, they do not count against fleet supply in that system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do ground forces fighting with the Nekro Virus flagship work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;They take part in the space combat as if they were ships.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (greghouse, Dec 29, 2017): &ldquo;Can i have the ground forces number over my fleet pool? &hellip; 1) Yes&rdquo; The Alastor ground forces do not count against the fleet pool.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has one of their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> tokens on the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan II faction unit upgrade technology, they may use <i>The Alastor</i> to have their PDS in the active system participate in the space combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A ground force participating in a space combat may count toward scoring the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Demonstrate%20Your%20Power"><i>Demonstrate Your Power</i></a> secret objective.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player loses their last ground force during a space combat and consequently meets the requirements for elimination, they are immediately eliminated. They will not be given the opportunity to score any objectives from winning the combat or destroying certain units at the same time their last ground force was destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Nekro player uses a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy an opponent&rsquo;s flagship, they may score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Destroy%20their%20Greatest%20Ship"><i>Destroy Their Greatest Ship</i></a> secret objective, even if there are some hits remaining that will cause the Nekro player to be eliminated once they are assigned. If this would bring the Nekro player to ten victory points, they will instead win the game before they are eliminated.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nekro-malleon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Malleon">Nekro Malleon</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the chosen player is the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player with their commander, Magmus, unlocked, they will gain a trade good from it if they spend a token from their strategy pool when resolving this ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>That trade good will be gained separately from the other two.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The ability of Nekro Malleon cannot be resolved while another ability is resolving.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can I use the Nekro Virus&rsquo; Agent, Nekro Malleon &hellip; to interrupt another ability since the timing is &lsquo;during the action phase&rsquo;? A: No, any ability that is used &lsquo;during the action phase&rsquo; cannot be resolved unless there are no other abilities currently being resolved.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="nekro-acidos"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Acidos">Nekro Acidos</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the Nekro player gains their third technology and unlocks Nekro Acidos, they cannot apply Nekro Acidos to that instance of gaining a technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Nekro commander draw an action card for the very technology that unlocks it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; unlock conditions are checked only after the current effect fully resolves.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the Nekro player places a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> token on a technology, they are not gaining a technology.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="polymorphic-algorithm">UNIT.DSGN.FLAYESH &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Polymorphic%20Algorithm">Polymorphic Algorithm</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the other player&rsquo;s units are destroyed, this does not trigger the Nekro player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Technological%20Singularity"><sc>Technological Singularity</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Unit upgrades do not have a color. The Nekro player cannot gain a unit upgrade with <i>Polymorphic Algorithm</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.8b: &ldquo;Unit upgrades do not have a color.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What counts for technology-colour objectives like Diversify Research and Master the Sciences?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Unit upgrades have no colour&rdquo; unit upgrades are colorless; Polymorphic Algorithm gain is by color.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="mordred"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Mech:~:text=Mordred">Mordred</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A Mordred will apply +2 against a player with both <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> tokens, and not +4.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="valefar-assimilator-z"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Breakthrough:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator%20Z">Valefar Assimilator Z</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Nekro player places a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> X or Y token on the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Flagship:~:text=Memoria"><i>Memoria II</i></a> unit upgrade technology card, their flagship would still gain each ability granted to them by <i>Valefar Assimilator Z</i> from the flagships of other players.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Nekro player cannot place multiple Valefar Assimilator Z tokens on the same player&rsquo;s faction sheet.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Placing a Valefar Assimilator Z token is not gaining a technology. It does not trigger the ability of Nekro Acidos, the Nekro player&rsquo;s commander.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With the Nekro breakthrough, can the flagship copy several other flagships, and what does it copy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It isn&rsquo;t a technology, so the Nekro commander doesn&rsquo;t trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player&rsquo;s faction sheet, they will always apply the +2 to the combat rolls for <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s faction sheet, copying their flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Terror%20Between"><i>The Terror Between</i></a>, they will capture destroyed units. They may also capture their own units, and may return their own captured units to their reinforcements at any time.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What is the interaction when Nekro has Vuil&rsquo;raith&rsquo;s flagship &hellip;? A: Nekro can capture their own units and can decide to return them to reinforcements at any time.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player copies the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Firmament_/_The_Obsidian#Flagship:~:text=Heaven%27s%20Eye"><i>Heaven&rsquo;s Eye</i></a>, references to &ldquo;your plots&rdquo; refer to the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s plots.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;If the Nekro Virus copies the Firmament flagship, can they somehow utilize its ability (it says &lsquo;1 of your plots&rsquo;)? A: Nekro references the Firmaments plots when copying the Firmament flagship.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Nekro player has copied the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, and the <a href="/F_firmament">Firmament</a> becomes the <a href="/F_firmament">Obsidian</a>, the Valefar Assimilator Z token is moved to the <a href="/F_firmament">Obsidian</a> player&rsquo;s flagship.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What happens with the Z ability on the Firmament flagship when they become Obsidian? A: The Z token is moved to the Obsidian Flagship.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Nekro player&rsquo;s flagship gains only the text abilities of a copied flagship. Unit abilities, such as <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a>, <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> or <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a>, are not copied.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With the Nekro breakthrough, can the flagship copy several other flagships, and what does it copy?&rdquo;: &ldquo;your flagship gains that flagship&rsquo;s text abilities &hellip; Unit abilities like Deploy, Space Cannon or Sustain Damage aren&rsquo;t text abilities, so copying flagships that rely on them gains nothing.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is eliminated while the Nekro player has a Valefar Assimilator Z token on their faction sheet, the Nekro player keeps the copied flagship abilities; that faction sheet remains in play for this purpose.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Does the Nekro Virus keep the faction flagship abilities of eliminated players? A: Yes, this follows other rulings on components that stay in play after a player is eliminated, those player&rsquo;s faction sheets remain in play for this ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
